    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d692">

                <pb facs="0807" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.67/11–248: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-02T16:00:00+08:00">November 2, 1948—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 2—4:38 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2292. Deptel 1843, 1st, 1 [<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p. m., repeated Moscow
                    1282. Local Soviet Consulate advises steamer available about November 15 for
                    Vladivostok. Koval and Bernhardt<anchor n="21" xml:id="d692-f1"/> visas
                    requested, personal data <pb facs="0808" n="798" xml:id="pg798"/> at Embassy
                    Moscow. Trip feasible if Soviet Foreign Office authorizes Soviet Consulate
                    Shanghai issue visas by November 10.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2292; repeated Moscow 33, Dairen 87, pouched Nanking 1735.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d692-f1" n="21" xml:id="d692-f1-content">
                <p>John Koval and Matthias R. Bernhardt, respectively, chosen to go as couriers to
                    Dairen.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
